Lines showing partition and offset as records are processed:
p0 @ 0: {"order_id": 4001}
p0 @ 1: {"order_id": 4002}
p1 @ 57: {"order_id": 4003}
Because on_assign seeks partition 0 to the beginning, p0 replays from offset 0 while other partitions resume from their committed positions.
